.TH TOOTLES 1 "November 2026" "Tootles 0.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
tootles \- a keyboard-first Mastodon and Bluesky client for the terminal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tootles
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B tootles login
.I instance
.RI [ --token-stdin ]
.br
.B tootles
.RI { accounts | switch | logout | theme | doctor | completions }
.SH DESCRIPTION
Tootles provides Mastodon and Bluesky timelines, search, notifications, threads,
profiles, posting, media, multiple accounts, and private local drafts.
Polls, lists, editing, and visibility options depend on the active network.
Without an account, it starts an interactive offline demo.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --demo
Open the offline playground without using saved credentials.
.TP
.B --theme NAME
Choose tokyo-night, midnight, paper, or contrast.
.TP
.B --config-dir DIRECTORY
Use a separate directory for credentials, preferences, and drafts.
.TP
.B --no-motion
Disable visual transitions.
.TP
.B --no-mouse
Do not capture mouse events; preserve terminal text selection.
.TP
.B --image-protocol halfblocks
Skip image capability queries and render previews as Unicode half blocks.
.TP
.B --snapshot FILE
Render an offline demo to an SVG or text file without a terminal.
.SH BLUESKY
.B tootles login --provider bluesky your-handle.bsky.social
prompts for a dedicated Bluesky app password without echoing it. The password is
used once and is not saved; access and refresh tokens are saved privately.
Use --pds URL for another account host and --app-password-stdin for standard input.
Press a to switch between saved Mastodon and Bluesky accounts. Drafts are separate.
Bluesky supports public posts and images; unavailable network features are hidden.
.SH KEYS
j/k or arrow keys move; 1 through 6 select timelines; n composes; r replies;
f favorites; b boosts; s bookmarks; Enter opens a thread; p opens a profile;
a switches accounts; m opens media; x reveals hidden content; v votes;
L lists links in the selected post; o opens the post in your browser;
Backspace or the left arrow returns to the previous view;
/ searches; Ctrl+K opens the command palette; ? opens help; q quits.
.PP
In the composer, Tab changes fields, F2 changes visibility, F3 browses files, Alt+A attaches the selected file and alt text,
F4 or Ctrl+Enter publishes, Ctrl+S saves, and Escape saves and closes the draft.
.SH MEDIA
The gallery uses available Kitty, Sixel, or iTerm2 graphics protocols, with a
half-block fallback. Media downloads begin only when the gallery is opened.
Local files can be previewed from the attachment browser with p.
For images, v cycles Terminal, Default image viewer, and Browser modes; Enter
opens the selected mode. Local images offer Terminal and Default image viewer.
The default viewer receives the original file with its full resolution.
Alacritty uses the pixelated block preview; choose the default viewer for detail.
For video and audio, v cycles Window, Terminal, and Browser modes; Enter plays.
Window and Terminal modes require an optional mpv installation.
In terminal playback, q returns to Tootles. The o key opens online originals
with the desktop URL handler, or local images in the default image viewer.
Default image viewing requires a desktop file association and xdg-open on Linux,
open on macOS, or the Windows file handler. Original image copies are held in a
private image-previews directory under the configuration directory, capped at
16 files / 256 MiB and pruned after 24 hours on the next use. Recent files are
kept for at least 10 minutes so asynchronous viewers have time to load them.
.SH FILES
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/tootles/config.toml
or
.I ~/.config/tootles/config.toml
contains preferences and plaintext access tokens. Unix files are private (0600)
and the directory is private (0700). Account-specific drafts are stored alongside.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.B TOOTLES_CONFIG_DIR
selects a configuration directory.
.B TOOTLES_TOKEN
supplies an existing Mastodon token to the login command.
.B NO_COLOR
selects high contrast and disables transitions.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR xdg-open (1)
